"Cell_line":"HaCaT","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"79.32 ± 0.83","IC50_Dark_value":79.32,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.3390/molecules27061897","Year":2022,"Counterion":"[Cl-]","Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":6,"value":-0.8077,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.3390/molecules27061897","year":2022,"counterion":"[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-004674","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Experimental 1-octanol/water partition coefficients (Po/w) were determined with the slow-stirring method [26], and 1-octanol and Mili-Q water were mutually saturated prior to their use. The arene Ru(II) complex of a known concentration in mixture (water saturated with 1-octanol and 1-octanol saturated with water) was shaken for 24 h on an oscillator. The solution was centrifuged for 5 min at 2500 rpm to allow the phase separation. The amount of ruthenium present in the saturated aqueous solution and saturated 1-octanol solution was measured through UV–vis spectroscopy [27], Here, the 1-octanol/water partition coefficient (logPo/w) is defined as the logarithm of the ratio between the molar concentration of complex in the octanol-rich phase(Co) and the molar concentration of complex in the water-rich phase(C): logPo/w = logCo/C"}]}